A||||22||kornholio||painting grey interior trim
Z||000000||kornholio||08-21-99||09:50 PM||||I've been thinking of painting the grey pieces of my Fiero interior black (my car is also black).  Has anyone else done this and does it look alright?  And should I use a flat black or a gloss black paint?  Your opinions are welcome.  Thanks.
Z||000001||terryk||08-21-99||11:25 PM||||I have. Works great. Get vinyl paint using the interior code from the RPO label. The paint store can put it in a can or give you a propellant can.<p>Get some vinyl prep (like a soap) that roughen ups the vinyl before you paint.<p>Use multiple light coats to avoid filling n the texture. It will not fill MAJOR gouges.<p>Works like a champ.
Z||000002||terryk||08-21-99||11:26 PM||||One other point. It works so good, I don't worry about the color of parts I get from the wrecker. I just paint them to match.  
Z||000003||Eric||08-22-99||11:43 AM||||I painted my black GT's interior black a few months ago and it looks great!  I'm planning on putting black seats and black carpet in too.  Try semi gloss or satin.
Z||000004||biggdaddy||08-22-99||01:11 PM||||What did you guys use to apply the paint? I was just thinking the same thing for my Fiero. I`ve got a pair of black and red mister mike`s coming and I plan on doing the carpeting myself.
Z||000005||kornholio||08-22-99||01:39 PM||||I was just thinking of painting the grey screw-on pieces like the panels that go over the speedo, gauges and radio.
Z||000006||biggdaddy||08-22-99||03:52 PM||||Beavis, That probably wouldn`t work as well as the vinyl parts...It would look cheap. The Fiero store sells replacement CARBON-FIBER faceplates that look great. There well worth the couple of dollars they cost.
Z||000007||kornholio||08-22-99||04:02 PM||||"There well worth the couple of dollars they cost"---Dude, they cost $349.  Now I don't know about your income, but that is way out of my league.
Z||000008||Eric||08-22-99||04:07 PM||||I paid about $180 for my faux carbon trim.  Since then, I've heard of a guy selling the same kit for less than $100.  I forgot his name but I know someone on this forum has bought a kit from him.
Z||000009||yellowFormula||08-22-99||04:08 PM||||Disagreed bigdaddy, it doesn't look cheap. I have seen a 86 SE with the trim painted red to match the color of the car and it looked great. I will do this to mine when I can find the yellow paint to match, I am still looking. And if you don't like it , flip it over and use the  other un-spraypainted side. No loss but about 7 bucks for a can of spraypaint, better then 350 bucks for some carbon fiber.
Z||000010||Gokart||08-22-99||05:51 PM||||I just did all my faceplates with wood grain shelf liner and then clear coated them. Everyone who sees them thinks I spent big bucks on a replacement wood grain kit! Instead of paying 349.00, I paid 1.99 for shelf liner and quality clear coat I already had! When Cliff changes things I'll post pictures.
Z||000011||kornholio||08-22-99||05:55 PM||||So glossy paint doesn't look good on the interior?  I was just thinking I could use the leftover touch-up paint that I have.
Z||000012||terryk||08-22-99||07:24 PM||||Use the vinyl paint. A pint will cost you around $35 and last longer than the car.<p><br>The Vinyl paint will work on hard and soft pieces. You could repaint the dash pad with the stuff. IT covers scuffs really well.<br>
Z||000013||GREENDANO||08-22-99||07:42 PM||||Gocart you win for the low dollar approach.  I got my cabon fiber dash kit from Dennis La Grua.  dlagrua@rcn.com<br>$89!!  It looks great, I painted my dash pieces yellow to match my car before I applied the trim pieces.  Pretty cool looking.  Here's his URL<br>http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm
Z||000014||kornholio||08-22-99||08:59 PM||||Does anyone have pics of their painted interior they could send me?
Z||000015||lowCG||08-22-99||10:30 PM||||I use the product called "Mar-Hyde",$5 a can,works very good,wears well.Two cans will do the entire interior.<br>The real carbon kits are expensive and I think the fake ones are about as good looking as contact paper.<br>I'm hoping that someone will make some good ones for le$$ someday.
Z||000016||GREENDANO||08-23-99||01:21 PM||||GO TO THE URL I POSTED!!  THEY LOOK GREAT, and they don't look like contact paper.  I spoke with Dennis and he says it's the same kit as the $350 kit from the rip-off Fiero store.  They are backed by 3-M tape and hold like mad.<br>  Dan-O
