Z||000020||BENGAL4||09-01-99||07:00 AM||||Gokart, what type of clearcoat did you use? I tried a clear vinyl paint from Mar Hyde and it looks Ok but I think it could look much better. Putting the contact paper on was easy. Just trim with an Exato knife. 
Z||000021||Gokart||09-02-99||04:38 AM||||Use over the counter Dupli-color super laquer first, two light coats, let dry over night. Then get the three part mix (econo-clear, reducer, hardener) and a $7.00 sprayer, put on two light coats, again let dry overnight. The mix is too harsh to put directly on the liner so be sure to use the over the counter laquer first. Good luck!
Z||000022||lowCG||09-02-99||11:09 AM||||The Mar-Hyde won't look glossy,like you'd want over wood,but be careful spraying laquer over it; it'll probably curdle,lift,and peel,you may need to remove the Mar-Hyde before putting laquer over the panels(or just start over).<br>Was just thinking that Hammerite,black(metallic)would look neat.
